2026-09-28 -- K04b continuous-refill control, NOT original failure closure.

The new C case replenishes completed requests immediately instead of waiting
for a full batch. It retains null devices, 4-KiB direct writes, depths 1/16 and
1/2 queues. Each case checks 16,384 identities, object addresses, lengths and
unique completions; only depth one requires order. Null writes do not establish
persistence. No original assertion or source is changed.

GCC14 and Clang19 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror compilation PASS in sealed ARM64.
GCC-built probe on retained GCC/EvoCC kernels: 4/4 cases and 65,536 complete
writes per Image PASS. All eight combinations show zero displaced/backward
completions. Replenishment alone does not reproduce the original fio/trace
failure; K04b remains OPEN.

Both nonce-bound HVF boot/shutdowns PASS; both runtime backing hashes unchanged.
The 1.6-MiB payload uses shared init and no new runtime disk. A separate kernel
recovery job was active; no performance inference. Older Images do not inherit
current compiler repairs. Image/runtime identities: kernel-uniform-selected-runtime.out.

